VALUES ('fa07ac89-9d4b-4ba8-94fd-a69ff01bd695', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000400', 'To free their citizens arrested by Tewodros, the British sent in late 1867, a large military expedition commanded by Sir Robert Napier. With the help of local allies who had their ambitions and grievances against Tewodros, such as Kasa Mercha of Tigray (the future Emperor Yohannes IV), the British were able to make their march from the coast to the interior. On 10 April 1868, up to 8,000 Tewodros’ soldiers, including his general Gebriye tried to check the advancing British forces but were defeated at the battle of Aroge. The following day, on 11 April 1868, Tewodros released his European captives and on 13 April, 1868, Tewodros committed suicide at Maqdala. This was followed by the burning of his fortress and looting of treasures.', 'G10-History-STB-2023-web.pdf p.1', '2026.1', 'published', '[0.000068326255,0.01124059,0.006371841,-0.0067108,-0.044296775,0.00574957,-0.030192148,-0.007094384,-0.006449333,-0.1133133,-0.03005475,0.007529532,0.0560212,0.039027877,-0.040320363,-0.035111554,-0.005704132,0.00009234809,0.05876341,-0.00707126,0.025362343,-0.016601967,-0.0030639882,-0.0016230432,-0.022210548,-0.0066090436,-0.01997898,-0.048349213,0.015165711,0.20462099,-0.060580518,-0.02221324,0.020911986,-0.006905019,0.0036408412,-0.007644215,-0.0032180983,0.02842124,0.032073524,-0.038387425,0.046913475,0.011121804,-0.010855176,0.0070842695,0.054088157,-0.026423823,-0.0035015438,0.01099967,0.012958534,0.026027406,-0.0035808645,-0.0112795085,0.025776561,-0.03052705,0.031603668,0.027759625,-0.014976149,-0.046789885,0.08189572,-0.0066616195,-0.017920533,-0.044465378,0.016392823,0.040179305,-0.07681897,0.021954397,0.017170519,-0.029770246,0.029826974,0.010883174,0.03814914,-0.007408773,0.025420079,0.023021823,-0.030471178,0.02128423,-0.069293365,0.010618821,0.033818766,0.0126477,0.022925608,-0.0040398594,-0.007956128,0.02606264,0.021290088,-0.010778094,-0.019061226,0.0021192643,0.008776175,0.