VALUES ('462a4524-ddca-4d3f-bb6f-cd1104a72023', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000400', 'Mussolini succeeded in expanding Italian territories. Aggressive Foreign Policy: Mussolini adopted an ambitious foreign policy and persuaded Yugoslavia to hand over the port of Fiume and acquired it in 1924. He established a protectorate over Albania in 1926 and subsequently annexed it in 1939. He also acquired some territory in East Africa and near Libya through negotiations with England and France. He conquered Ethiopia in 1936, which sounded a death knell of the League of Nations. Led to Second World War: Mussolini joined the Anti-Communist Pact of Germany and Japan in 1937. Thus came into being the Berlin-Tokyo-Rome Axis. During the Spanish Civil War, Italy helped General Franco. The victory of the General in the Civil War strengthened the position of Italy in the western Mediterranean. What conditions in post-World War I Italy favoured the rise of Fascism? ', 'G10-History-STB-2023-web.pdf p.1', '2026.1', 'published', '[0.0019189203,0.024909357,-0.028786518,0.0022749335,0.032117788,-0.01593087,-0.01666552,0.041250005,-0.013347793,-0.09373789,-0.016591437,0.04667808,0.05830443,-0.016196366,-0.0252762,-0.033764567,0.029164169,-0.06380414,0.05765512,0.017894028,0.029144095,0.011647215,-0.019205457,0.030992463,-0.022473391,-0.005926768,-0.0036114333,-0.022733811,-0.017961122,0.19920805,0.0072977305,-0.0054452815,0.024404613,0.013218162,0.008286307,0.016115898,-0.030551054,-0.012662762,-0.0025773023,-0.041690554,0.0133768385,0.025077105,0.012123041,0.040185682,0.035077825,-0.020506544,-0.03931357,0.06284694,0.008059841,-0.0074947565,-0.008088735,0.0024019966,-0.031591795,-0.075990036,0.038242657,0.024815239,0.03015517,0.0245412,0.084534764,-0.012560966,0.008240611,0.005216934,-0.013467036,0.025974149,-0.035062663,-0.016875401,0.005420767,-0.04231612,0.05054764,0.0025568632,0.042113714,0.031878915,0.022553414,0.008302617,-0.040842075,0.010484068,-0.04525197,0.013111678,0.05449453