VALUES ('f73cc4c1-d9d8-4001-9d6e-d1cfaa80e532', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000400', 'The Secretariat Generals of the UNO Trygvie Lie of Norway1946-52 Dag Hammarskjöld of Sweden1952-61 U Thant of Myanmar, Burma1961-71 Kurt Waldheim of Austria1971-81 Javier Perez de Cuellar of Peru1981-91 Boutros Boutros-Ghali of Egypt1991-96 Kofi Anan of Ghana1997-2006 Ban Ki-Moon of South Korea2007-2016 Antonio Gutierrez of Portugalsince January 2017 4.Trusteeship Council:- Trusteeship Council aims at helping countries under foreign rule to attain independence. Eleven such countries came under this system after the Second World War. By 1994, all Trust Territories had attained independence. The last to do was Palau. 5.International Court of Justice:- The International Court of Justice is the principal judicial organ of the UN. The seat of the Court is in The Hague, Netherlands. It is composed of 15 judges elected by the General Assembly. 6.The Economic and Social Council (ECOSOC) assists the General Assembly in promoting international economic and social cooperation and development. 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 History Grade 10 Student Textbook Exercise and Activity', 'G10-History-STB-2023-web.pdf p.1', '2026.1', 'published', '[0.0018431009,0.035508752,-0.0047977846,-0.019803246,0.046378784,-0.010318258,-0.018259779,0.0008775044,0.00963687,-0.103664674,-0.059795864,0.010242841,0.0053075873,0.008969491,-0.04265741,-0.06666318,0.008199218,0.0010970079,0.01122039,-0.014921317,0.054213904,-0.009939712,0.0023247327,-0.013613645,-0.053024814,0.003031796,-0.0040961583,-0.020081172,0.022507893,0.21372372,-0.022627013,-0.022906026,-0.025864037,-0.0023093668,-0.03680974,-0.008203127,0.0061882758,-0.03314872,-0.0035006655,-0.023853637,-0.013747932,-0.01499074,0.014263975,0.028445603,-0.011323453,-0.044776704,-0.034432486,0.02946862,0.023540782,0.02313805,0.034489095,0.03547845,0.012126811,-0.011855566,0.015605215,0.05719576,-0.00040636904,-0.012392927,0.007545283,0.057892054,-0.00075384986,0.03562155,0.